  "notes": "Drawn from one dated photo of N581UW (left side, 2026-04-07); the Commons category has no other photo in this scheme. Base reads white above the cheatline; under it the fuselage darkens towards the belly, which may be a light gray lower fuselage or only shade: not drawn as a split. Belly, wing undersides and the right side not seen. Small 'Piedmont Pacemaker' script by the nose is too small to read reliably and is left out. Sources disagree on whether N581UW is Piedmont or PSA; dated Commons photos (Piedmont N581UW Apr 2026; PSA N582UW Nov 2025) settle it. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N581UW (2026-04-07): 'American' x 0.194-0.284 as drawn; 'A321' on the fin fills the gap in the blue pinstripes (x 0.30-0.63); 'PIEDMONT' left as drawn (the photo is a climbing three-quarter view: its ends read 0.12-0.85 of the chord, within the error of the view). The cheatline's rounded nose drawn as a curve. No measured A321 shape yet.",
  "history": "Previously on A319 N744P."
